{"title":"Imaginary unit","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>imaginary unit</b>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/9/75952e52a3dc061d24146c0df9062a54a5ce5a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i=\\sqrt{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" />, is the fundamental component of all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_numbers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Complex numbers\">complex numbers</a>. In fact, it is a complex number itself. It has a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Magnitude\" title=\"Magnitude\">magnitude</a> of 1, and can be written as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1deb4f301ba18baf24a42745241ecea64351d98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\text{cis } \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"74\" height=\"35\" />. Any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_number\" title=\"Complex number\">complex number</a> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/5/615e780fda439b2829922a704a60b31c5ed77191.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> for some real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Trigonometric_function_cis\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Trigonometric function cis</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Series\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Series</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Use_in_factorization\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Use in factorization</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Trigonometric_function_cis\">Trigonometric function cis</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_unit&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Trigonometric function cis\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<dl><dd><i>Main article: <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cis\" title=\"Cis\">cis</a></i></dd></dl>\n<p>The trigonometric function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/2/8628735d756abfd8e0820430fd86db47af95d61b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{cis } x$\" width=\"34\" height=\"11\" /> is also defined as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/0/3a05bb2d3214a6f7d27a70c01fb6cb2dbae72138.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{ix}$\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bbedb72fb347d0516f749ea28d54105d589bfa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos x + i\\sin x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Series\">Series</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_unit&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Series\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is used in an exponential series, it repeats at every four terms:\n</p>\n<ol><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a51bd6b7d88b41fce830214716979b79911f5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^1=\\sqrt{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/4/1949b1f9e784c8f6a4203e12fe2c55875bd090d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^2=\\sqrt{-1}\\cdot\\sqrt{-1}=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"174\" height=\"18\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/f/7df9f6406c862bfbef87307e7cac46f80d76e327.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^3=-1\\cdot i=-i$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/1/7d181f9e7c39245d73c2642c385d15bc3a827748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^4=-i\\cdot i=-i^2=-(-1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"238\" height=\"19\" /></li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/1/c8116ea6da32c59f1eb35ea59c0cbf0277453a08.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^5=1\\cdot i=i$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" /></li></ol>\n<p>This has many useful properties.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Use_in_factorization\">Use in factorization</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_unit&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Use in factorization\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is often very helpful in factorization. For example, consider the difference of squares: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7a54d6857592c5ce4ac8c2a7435d79f4840c3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+b)(a-b)=a^2-b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"185\" height=\"19\" />. With <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, it is possible to factor the otherwise-unfactorisable <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/6/cf669d58fbd0410ca860758e53606d06425a4d97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"16\" /> into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/2/0429270e88640c86a0243e047d5b20a3e0cf5018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a+bi)(a-bi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problems\">Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_unit&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_unit&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>Find the sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/e/9cee0c92e1b17ab2764590281ad8468001f5b89e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^1+i^2+\\ldots+i^{2006}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"147\" height=\"16\" /> (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_unit/Introductory\" title=\"Imaginary unit/Introductory\">Source</a>)</li>\n<li>Find the product of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/d/93dc33d5e444734109e677b54dd267d56a905245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^1 \\times i^2 \\times \\cdots \\times i^{2006}$\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />. (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_unit/Introductory\" title=\"Imaginary unit/Introductory\">Source</a>)</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_unit&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>The equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04d309c1bb4819c1b17b0b30725bfb1fe9d94a0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^6+z^3+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"16\" /> has complex roots with argument <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/4/c4460b5100c3ce982ab5ebb20a8c3871e9cfdc54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"13\" /> in the complex plane. Determine the degree measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1984_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1984 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">Source</a>)</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_unit&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/6/f566f68f3a44f3bfc58c8c5546a816c6fb97817d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\in\\mathcal M_2(R)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"91\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/c/f8ca6ff51b9f5da18dd249093e2132d236bc1772.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P\\in R[X]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"18\" /> with no real roots. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/e/ddea8ff0463c57bb606cc40a2c7c5cf9de7b9861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\det(P(A)) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"18\" /> , show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b1218308f04d43fe96b2152dab5667fa4e81e09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(A) = O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />. &lt;url&gt;viewtopic.php?t=78260 (Source)&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Imaginary_unit&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Algebra\" title=\"Algebra\">Algebra</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_numbers\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Complex numbers\">Complex numbers</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">Geometry</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Omega\" title=\"Omega\">Omega</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017093458\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.044 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 190/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 56/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 24/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5408/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   10.759      1 Template:Main\n100.00%   10.759      1 -total\n 45.68%    4.915      1 Template:Hatnote\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:1990:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017093458 and revision id 27796. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}